    "created_at": "2019-09-26T14:38:37Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-09-26T14:38:37Z",
    "body": "As a sort of aside, if possible, please give the ability to not display the number for at least deleted files status. (Per-status-state control of numbers even?)\r\n\r\nThe reason is libgit2 (which I believe starship uses, if I read cargo right). The main repository(ies) I work with day-to-day uses git sparse checkout and with a previous prompt I used (powerlevel10k), libgit2 goes a bit nuts. See https://github.com/romkatv/powerlevel10k/issues/127 referencing https://github.com/libgit2/libgit2/issues/2263\r\n\r\nMy brain is now pretty much used to seeing this as a good prompt:\r\n```\r\n@NCEP_Shared on  HEAD [✘] \r\n❯ git status\r\nHEAD detached at v1.0.0\r\nnothing to commit, working tree clean\r\n```\r\nand ignoring the red X as, well, there are no deleted files. Rather we've sparse-checkout'd a few directories but libgit2 sees them as deleted files. ",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
